    "https://faculty-clarkson.icims.com/jobs/1135/assistant-or-associate-professor---tenure-track/job?in_iframe=1": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Tenure Track ID 2024-1135 Posted Date 2 years ago (2/12/2025 1:25 PM) Visa Sponsorship Eligible No Hybrid Role No Pay Range USD $93,000.00 - USD $106,500.00 /Yr. Overview The Computer Science Department at Clarkson University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We are a small department where faculty are passionate about both teaching and research. We are interested in candidates who share this passion and are committed to excellence in both teaching and research. We seek candidates with expertise in any area of computer science but are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in artificial intelligence and cybersecurity. Department faculty have research expertise in artificial intelligence, robotics, computer systems, cybersecurity, algorithmic accountability, theoretical computer science, and quantum computing. Their research has been supported by NSF, the Office of Naval Research and the National Security Agency, among others. They have also served on policy committees of the ACM and IEEE, an advisory council of NSF, and on assessment panels of the Army Research Lab. Responsibilities • Teach a variety of undergraduate and graduate computer science courses. • Develop and sustain a research program. • Advise and mentor both undergraduate and graduate students. • Provide service to the Department, University and Profession. Qualifications Minimum: A Ph.D. in Computer Science or a related field by the start date. A publication record and the strong potential to secure external funding. Preferred: Teaching experience. Physical Demands The physical demands characteristics described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Health & Safety Health & 